{"id":8194788,"docketId":65292570,"caseName":"Louisiana v. Cummins","caseNameFull":"Louisiana v. Cummins","slug":"louisiana-v-cummins","docketNumber":"","dateFiled":"1941-10-20","dateArgued":null,"dateCertGranted":null,"year":1941,"scdbId":"","direction":"","votesMajority":null,"votesMinority":null,"disposition":"","posture":"","syllabus":null,"summary":null,"headnotes":null,"proceduralHistory":null,"attorneys":"Messrs. Eugene Stanley, Attorney General of Louisiana, and James J. Morrison for plaintiff. Messrs. Roger Siddall and Eberhard P. Deutsch for Claude Cum-mins et al., and Mr. Bon Geaslin for Abraham L. Shushan, defendants.","natureOfSuit":"","citationCount":2,"judges":"","jurisdictionType":"","opinions":[{"id":8156723,"type":"majority","typeCode":"020lead","perCuriam":false,"author":"","joinedBy":"","pageCount":null,"textLength":1321,"isHtml":true,"text":"<opinion type=\"majority\">\n<author id=\"Ap9f\">\n<em>Per Curiam:</em>\n</author>\n<p id=\"ANqA\">Leave to file the complaint is denied for want of jurisdiction, it appearing that one of the named parties defendant is a citizen of Louisiana. <em>California </em>v. <em>Southern Pacific Co., </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"9417682\"><a href=\"/opinion/94157/california-v-southern-pacific-co/#256\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: California v. Southern Pacific Co.\">157 U. S. 229, 256-262</a></span>; <em>Minnesota </em>v. <em>Northern Securities Co., </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"95591\"><a href=\"/opinion/95591/minnesota-v-northern-securities-co/#238\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Minnesota v. Northern Securities Co.\">184 U. S. 199, 238</a></span>; <em>New Mexico </em>v. <em>Lane, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"98876\"><a href=\"/opinion/98876/state-of-new-mexico-v-lane/#58\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: State of New Mexico v. Lane\">243 U. S. 52, 58</a></span>; <em>Texas </em>v. <em>Interstate Commerce Commission, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"99935\"><a href=\"/opinion/99935/texas-v-interstate-commerce-commission/#163\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Texas v. Interstate Commerce Commission\">258 U. S. 158, 163</a></span>. The rule to show cause is discharged.</p>\n</opinion>"}],"citations":[]}